(*
expect:
fired 1
last 5
peek 5
overruns 4
done
*)
(* tuvm#20 — a CELL under pressure COALESCES (G2's latest-value case), with zero
   new API: choosing `put:` at rung 9 WAS choosing latest-value semantics, so the
   overflow policy derives from the kind. A cell's queued ring events are doorbell
   pokes — the value is already in the slot — so collapsing them loses nothing a
   cell ever promised: `peek:` answers the latest value and the reader gets at
   least one poke.

   Trace (depth 64): put sp=1 (the cell's poke occupies slot 1), fill the
   remaining 63 slots with stream posts to `filler` (no reaction registered —
   drained-and-dropped later, but they hold the ring full NOW), then 4 more puts
   (sp=2..5). Each finds the ring full and coalesces into the cell's own queued
   poke — the poke's payload becomes 5, no new slot, 4 overruns counted. Drain:
   the reaction fires ONCE with the LAST value. N puts under overload -> one
   firing with the latest value, and the fires-on-WRITE guarantee (16_cells/04)
   yielded only at overflow, observably.

   Below the overflow line nothing changes: 16_cells/04 still pins 3 puts ->
   3 fires when the ring has room. *)
class CellCoalesce packageUsing: manifest = ( | fired ::= 0. last ::= nil. | ) (
  public main: platform args: args = (
    | space pid filler |
    space:: platform space.
    pid::    space channel: 'pid'.
    filler:: space channel: 'filler'.
    pid whenever: 'sp' do: [ :v | fired:: fired + 1. last:: v ].
    pid put: 'sp' value: 1.
    1 to: 63 do: [ :i | filler out: '' value: i ].
    2 to: 5 do: [ :i | pid put: 'sp' value: i ].
    space drain.
    ('fired ' , fired printString) out.
    ('last ' , last printString) out.
    ('peek ' , (pid peek: 'sp' ifAbsent: [ 0 ]) printString) out.
    ('overruns ' , (platform spaceOverruns: 'pid/sp') printString) out.
    'done' out.
  )
) : (
)
